! Validation roles: P6/P7 are the primary background-normalized code-validation
! channels. P8/P9 exact states are retained as diagnostics until detector-response
! folding is implemented; they do not control the default model/data PASS/FAIL gate.
!
! =============================================================================
! AMPS Earth validation C10 GRIDDED branch:
!   POES/MetOp MEPED proton-access-boundary storm validation
!
! Scientific observable
! ---------------------
! During the December 2006 storm the equatorward edge of the polar proton-access
! region (the "SEP cutoff boundary") observed by POES/MetOp SEM-2 MEPED moves
! equatorward, becomes MLT-asymmetric, and recovers.  C10 reproduces that
! boundary from first principles: for each storm interval it evaluates one or
! more IGRF+T05/TS05 field snapshots on a global 850-km geodetic shell and
! backtraces vertically incident protons at the four validation rigidities
! (0.174, 0.262, 0.369, 0.531 GV, mapped from the nominal P6-P9 lower
! thresholds 16, 36, 70, and 140 MeV).  The runner normally reconstructs a
! common ACCESS_T50 boundary from the exact-rigidity access states: resolved
! allowed fractions are evaluated in each MLT sector, fitted with weighted
! isotonic regression, and interpolated at transmission T=0.5.  FULL_SCAN also
! retains Rc_lower, Rc_effective, and Rc_upper as diagnostics.  The resulting
! MLT boundaries are summarized with a first-harmonic polar-boundary fit; this
! compact diagnostic is not the full five-parameter geometric ellipse of
! Dmitriev et al. (2010).
!
! Unlike PAMELA (C9), every ingredient of the POES comparison is public: the
! MEPED fluxes, the sub-satellite position (no attitude/ephemeris needed), and
! the field driver reuse the same checksum-verified five-minute TS05 event
! driver bundled with C9.  C10 does not need any nonpublic spacecraft data.
!
! This is the Mode3D/GRIDDED companion to AMPS_PARAM_C10_gridless.in.  The
! runner can select FULL_SCAN (PENUMBRA_SCAN plus companion exact-rigidity
! states) or the much faster GRIDDED-only DIRECT_ACCESS (RIGIDITY_LIST inside the
! configured latitude band).  Both products use the same driver, epochs, shell
! geometry, rigidity list, mover, and trajectory limits.  This
! branch first samples IGRF+T05 on the standalone Mode3D AMR mesh and then
! evaluates the field along trajectories through the interpolation stencil.
! Comparing both branches isolates mesh/interpolation sensitivity.  The runner
! copies this template into
! every snapshot directory and changes only named directives (EPOCH, DRIVER_FILE,
! rigidity list/energy bracket, scan count, shell spacing, access-latitude band,
! and trace time).  The generated input and full command are archived per run.
! =============================================================================

#CALCULATION_MODE
CALC_TARGET             CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
FIELD_EVAL_METHOD       GRID_3D

#CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
! Default bracket 0.05-1.30 GV for protons brackets the four MEPED-channel
! rigidities.  Kinetic-energy limits are written explicitly because the AMPS
! cutoff parser accepts energy.
CUTOFF_EMIN             1.331292
CUTOFF_EMAX             664.960431
CUTOFF_MAX_PARTICLES    1
CUTOFF_NENERGY          50
CUTOFF_SAMPLING         VERTICAL
CUTOFF_SEARCH_ALGORITHM PENUMBRA_SCAN
CUTOFF_UPPER_SCAN_N     120
CUTOFF_SCAN_SPACING     LINEAR
! During FULL_SCAN, a non-empty rigidity list requests an additional access file
! classifying these exact rigidities; the Rc_lower/Rc_effective/Rc_upper full-
! shell scan is unchanged.  During DIRECT_ACCESS, the runner changes
! CUTOFF_SEARCH_ALGORITHM to RIGIDITY_LIST and traces only these four values in
! the configured latitude band.  The Python postprocessor computes ACCESS_T50
! identically from either exact-state product.
CUTOFF_RIGIDITY_LIST_GV 0.174013525,0.262395866,0.369131538,0.531334344
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MIN 45.0
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MAX 85.0
CUTOFF_TRACE_POLICY     ACCURATE
CUTOFF_BACKTRACE_CHARGE REVERSED
CUTOFF_TRACE_LIMIT_POLICY FORBIDDEN
CUTOFF_MAX_TRAJ_TIME    20.0

#PARTICLE_SPECIES
SPECIES                 PROTON
CHARGE                  1
MASS_AMU                1.007276466621

#BACKGROUND_FIELD
! The driver table is sampled once at EPOCH for each standalone snapshot run.
! The runner uses the checksum-verified driver bundled under C10/data by default.
FIELD_MODEL             T05
EPOCH                   2006-12-15T03:00:00
DRIVER_FILE             ts05_driver.txt
! Static values are parser-safe fallbacks only.  A loaded driver overrides them.
DST                     -100.0
PDYN                    4.0
IMF_BX                  0.0
IMF_BY                  0.0
IMF_BZ                  -5.0
SW_VX                   -450.0
SW_N                    5.0
T05_W1                  0.0
T05_W2                  0.0
T05_W3                  0.0
T05_W4                  0.0
T05_W5                  0.0
T05_W6                  0.0

#MODE3D_MESH
! Near-Earth resolution controls interpolation accuracy where the 850-km
! access boundary is determined.  The 0.02-Re near-Earth target is the
! production starting point; repeat C10 with 0.01 Re for mesh convergence.
MODE3D_MESH_RES_EARTH_RE     0.02
MODE3D_MESH_RES_BOUNDARY_RE  2.0
MODE3D_MESH_COARSENING       LINEAR
MODE3D_MESH_EXPONENT         1.0

#DOMAIN_BOUNDARY
! Bare lengths are kilometers.  +/-25 Re is large enough for the empirical
! magnetosphere used by this event-level access calculation.
DOMAIN_X_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_X_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MAX             159280.0
R_INNER                  6371.2

#SPECTRUM
! Required by the common parser; not used by cutoff-rigidity tracing.
SPECTRUM_TYPE           POWER_LAW
SPEC_J0                 1.0
SPEC_GAMMA              2.0
SPEC_E0                 1000.0
SPEC_EMIN               1.0
SPEC_EMAX               2000.0

#OUTPUT_DOMAIN
! Global geodetic shell at POES altitude.  The runner transforms retained nodes
! to AACGM latitude and MLT at the exact snapshot epoch and extracts the
! per-MLT, per-hemisphere access boundary.  SHELL_GEOMETRY=GEODETIC follows the
! current Earth cutoff-test convention.
OUTPUT_MODE             SHELLS
SHELL_COUNT             1
SHELL_ALTS_KM           850.0
SHELL_LON_RES_DEG       15.0
SHELL_LAT_RES_DEG       2.0
SHELL_GEOMETRY          GEODETIC

#OUTPUT_OPTIONS
OUTPUT_COORDS           GEO

#NUMERICAL
DT_TRACE                0.2
ADAPTIVE_DT             T
MAX_STEPS               500000
MAX_TRACE_TIME          20.0
MAX_TRACE_DISTANCE      400.0
TRAP_DETECTION          T

!#END
